WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:28.000
Nvidia's open platform now enforces agent guardrails in silicon from the first test run through full deployment. This is Models &amp; Agents, episode 188. The system combines OpenShell for external policy, Bluefield Ford DPUs, and DOKA software to create a host-independent layer. 100 firms have already joined the effort. The platform is available now for developers building agent fleets at enterprise scale.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:33.720
Trend AI extended the same platform with threat intelligence that informs policy boundaries

00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:36.600
across the model, harness, and tool layers.

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:42.980
Rachel Gin, chief platform and business officer at Trend AI, noted that security must cover

00:00:42.980 --> 00:00:44.840
every component and agent touches.

00:00:45.560 --> 00:00:52.780
Sonnet 5.5 runs more than 30% faster and costs up to 30% less than the prior Sonnet version,

00:00:53.120 --> 00:00:54.820
while beating it on every benchmark.

00:00:54.820 --> 00:01:01.460
mark. It is now the default model for the free tier at claw.ai. Free users can therefore

00:01:01.460 --> 00:01:06.920
run the same coding and animation experiments previously limited to paid accounts. Chat

00:01:06.920 --> 00:01:14.160
GPT's free tier still uses the less capable GPT 5.6 Luna model. Simon Willis and highlighted

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:20.340
that free tier users can now build three-dimensional WebGL animations that previously required paid

00:01:20.340 --> 00:01:26.220
access. OpenAI released a document outlining how it constructs safety cases for frontier

00:01:26.220 --> 00:01:30.800
reinforcement learning training runs. The guidelines cover technical safeguards,

00:01:31.220 --> 00:01:35.340
operational practices, and procedures for investigating misalignment incidents.

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:41.260
The approach requires documented arguments and evidence that each identified hazard is either

00:01:41.260 --> 00:01:47.580
eliminated or reduced below an acceptable threshold. OpenAI decided not to release a new frontier

00:01:47.580 --> 00:01:50.580
model after internal tests revealed safety issues.

00:01:51.140 --> 00:01:55.920
The decision follows similar pauses at other labs and comes after public statements from

00:01:55.920 --> 00:01:58.500
former researchers about extinction-level risks.

00:01:59.300 --> 00:02:03.720
Two new attention methods reduce redundant computation in long-context models.

00:02:04.460 --> 00:02:10.200
Co-Window distributes distant context across KV heads with complementary windows while sharing

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:12.060
local and prefix sync windows.

00:02:12.060 --> 00:02:17.680
mass-alloc uses softmax statistics to skip low contribution tiles after full

00:02:17.680 --> 00:02:25.220
causal QK scoring. At 128,000 tokens on 8H100 GPUs, the methods delivered

00:02:25.220 --> 00:02:31.360
forward speedups of 7.4 times and 2.2 times respectively versus full attention.

00:02:32.220 --> 00:02:39.580
Backward speedups reached 8.6 times for co-indo and 3.0 times for mass-alloc. At 14

00:02:39.580 --> 00:02:44.560
Building Billion Parameters with 32,000 context, the techniques reduced total training

00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:52.680
flops by 28.5%, and 23.1% while maintaining comparable capabilities on reported evaluations.

00:02:53.640 --> 00:02:59.780
Bloomberg released Enterprise Model Context Protocol, an AI Access Layer for Data License Plus.

00:03:00.260 --> 00:03:07.380
The protocol supplies AI-ready metadata, semantic context, and workflow-focused skills so agents

00:03:07.380 --> 00:03:12.420
Signations can interpret data across more than 100 million securities and 50,000 fields.

00:03:12.920 --> 00:03:17.940
Clients can now query in plain language and receive context-carrying results without

00:03:17.940 --> 00:03:19.880
manual identifier reconciliation.

00:03:20.740 --> 00:03:26.400
The solution targets research, portfolio, risk, and operations workflows in capital markets.

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:32.800
Microsoft added fabric apps, agentic data engineering features from the Osmos acquisition,

00:03:32.800 --> 00:03:37.460
and a monitor hub for proactive operations inside Microsoft fabric.

00:03:38.100 --> 00:03:43.000
Fabric apps lets teams build into and governed applications directly on one lake

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:44.700
without deploying containers.

00:03:45.420 --> 00:03:49.740
The new agentic engineering tools let users define an outcome and boundaries

00:03:49.740 --> 00:03:54.360
while an agent executes, validates, and refines the work autonomously.

00:03:55.020 --> 00:03:59.940
The monitor hub provides a unified view across jobs, capacities, work spaces

00:03:59.940 --> 00:04:02.760
and workloads to support proactive operations.

00:04:03.460 --> 00:04:06.840
GitHub researchers used an open-source AI security agent

00:04:06.840 --> 00:04:09.600
to discover 24 vulnerabilities in Android.

00:04:10.280 --> 00:04:12.520
The post details the targeted task flows

00:04:12.520 --> 00:04:13.700
that produce the findings

00:04:13.700 --> 00:04:16.720
and explains how developers can run the same agent

00:04:16.720 --> 00:04:18.120
against their own applications.

00:04:18.880 --> 00:04:21.500
The agent is released under an open-source license.

00:04:22.180 --> 00:04:24.320
MIT Media Lab published a framework

00:04:24.320 --> 00:04:27.120
mapping five levels of AI agent autonomy,

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:31.260
– drawing parallels to the SAE levels used for autonomous vehicles.

00:04:31.800 --> 00:04:37.200
The document provides a structured way to classify agent capabilities and required safeguards

00:04:37.200 --> 00:04:37.880
at each level.

00:04:38.400 --> 00:04:40.540
It is available on the Media Lab site.

00:04:41.220 --> 00:04:46.260
Hugging face released hollow 4, a model aimed at generalist computer use agents.

00:04:46.820 --> 00:04:51.540
The announcement includes details on training approach and intended use cases for agents that

00:04:51.540 --> 00:04:53.220
interact with graphical interfaces.

00:04:53.220 --> 00:04:57.940
The model and associated resources are hosted on the Hugging Face platform.

00:04:58.740 --> 00:05:03.700
Safety cases for frontier reinforcement learning runs require evidence that specific hazards

00:05:03.700 --> 00:05:07.340
have been controlled rather than relying on a single test score.

00:05:07.980 --> 00:05:13.200
The approach begins with hazard identification, then demands documented arguments and evidence

00:05:13.200 --> 00:05:18.520
that each hazard is either eliminated or its likelihood reduced below an acceptable threshold.

00:05:18.520 --> 00:05:23.880
controlled. Technical safeguards such as sandboxed execution and output filtering form one

00:05:23.880 --> 00:05:28.900
layer, while operational practices such as staged rollouts and independent review boards

00:05:28.900 --> 00:05:33.980
form another. When an incident occurs, the case must be updated with new evidence showing

00:05:33.980 --> 00:05:40.060
why the controls failed and how they were strengthened. The method forces teams to quantify uncertainty

00:05:40.060 --> 00:05:45.360
instead of claiming safety from the absence of observed failures. Teams should adopt this

00:05:45.360 --> 00:05:49.360
structure when the training run involves novel capabilities whose failure modes are

00:05:49.360 --> 00:05:50.880
not yet fully characterized.

00:05:51.580 --> 00:05:58.820
Try Sonnet 5.5 on the free tier at claw.ai for coding or animation tasks that previously

00:05:58.820 --> 00:06:00.180
required a paid account.

00:06:00.920 --> 00:06:06.680
Test the GitHub open source AI security agent against an Android app you maintain to surface

00:06:06.680 --> 00:06:09.220
vulnerabilities the same way the researchers did.

00:06:09.860 --> 00:06:15.160
Explore Bloomberg Enterprise MCP if you build financial agents that need context-rich

00:06:15.160 --> 00:06:18.320
data retrieval without manual identifier mapping.

00:06:19.020 --> 00:06:24.160
Run the co-window or mass-allogue attention implementations from the archive papers if

00:06:24.160 --> 00:06:28.960
you train or serve long-context models on multiple H100 GPUs.

00:06:29.480 --> 00:06:34.440
OpenAI DevDay takes place tomorrow, with expected announcements on new capabilities.

00:06:35.180 --> 00:06:39.320
Anthropic indicated HighCoo 5.5 will arrive in the coming weeks.

00:06:39.320 --> 00:06:44.600
More labs are expected to publish safety case frameworks following OpenAI's release.

00:06:45.200 --> 00:06:50.060
Pop the hood on safety cases for frontier reinforcement learning runs and the structure

00:06:50.060 --> 00:06:50.900
becomes clearer.

00:06:51.520 --> 00:06:56.600
The method starts by listing concrete hazards instead of claiming overall safety from passing

00:06:56.600 --> 00:06:57.060
a benchmark.

00:06:57.860 --> 00:07:02.600
Each hazard then needs a documented argument plus supporting evidence that the risk sits

00:07:02.600 --> 00:07:04.100
below an accepted threshold.

00:07:04.920 --> 00:07:11.800
Sandboxing and output filters supply one set of controls while staged rollouts and review boards supply another.

00:07:12.320 --> 00:07:18.080
An incident forces the entire case to be revised with fresh evidence on why the prior controls failed.

00:07:18.700 --> 00:07:26.740
Teams gain a decision rule here. Use the full safety case structure when training introduces capabilities whose failure modes remain poorly mapped.

00:07:27.400 --> 00:07:31.440
Narrow or fine-tuning projects can stay with simpler evaluation checklists.

